    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468-a1">

                <pb facs="0602" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fowle to Mr.
                            Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cesarea</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: You may, perhaps, recall our
                    conversation of May 23, regarding a request to the Department of State that the
                    British consul at Angora, H. S. Shipley, esq., be authorized officially to take
                    charge of any business pertaining to the Americans here at Oesarea that would
                    naturally come under the jurisdiction of an American consul if we had one in
                    this (Angora) vilayet.</p>
                <p>We hope and trust that no such occasion will arise, but agree with the opinion
                    expressed that day that it will be best to be prepared for emergencies.</p>
                <p>If the matter and the manner of this request meet with your approval, will you
                    kindly forward it to Washington through the regular channels?</p>
                <p>Assuring you that we fully appreciate the difficulties of your position and are
                    grateful for favors received,</p>
                <p>I remain, on behalf of the members of our mission, sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. L. Fowle.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
